<main class="shell"><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">INTTEGRO × RAILS</span><h1>Convention meets checkout.</h1><p>A conventional Rails controller calls the official Ruby SDK and keeps the merchant credential on the server.</p><dl><div><dt>Amount</dt><dd>GHS 50.00</dd></div><div><dt>Framework</dt><dd>Rails 8.1</dd></div></dl></section><section class="card"><span class="step">Demo order</span><h2>Integration workshop</h2><p class="muted">The hosted URL always comes from Inttegro.</p><% if @error_code.present? %><div class="error" role="alert"><strong><%= @error_code %></strong><span><%= @error_message %></span></div><% end %><%= form_with url: "/checkout", method: :post do |form| %><%= form.hidden_field :attempt_id, value: @attempt_id %><%= form.label :name do %>Name<%= form.text_field :name, value: "Akua Mensah", autocomplete: "name", required: true %><% end %><%= form.label :email do %>Email<%= form.email_field :email, value: "akua@example.com", autocomplete: "email", required: true %><% end %><%= form.label :phone do %>Phone<%= form.telephone_field :phone, value: "+233544998605", autocomplete: "tel", required: true %><% end %><%= form.button do %>Continue to Inttegro <span>→</span><% end %><% end %></section></main>
